From: ACK72 <acikom72@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: count only final TX failures in station statistics

The TX-free header carries each frame's transmission count and final
status. tx_failed added every retry to the final failure, so it equalled
tx_retries whenever no frame was lost and overstated real losses
otherwise. nl80211 defines TX_FAILED as failed packets, and mac80211
reports frames that failed after all retries. Count the final status only;
retries remain in tx_retries.

diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches/9999-zzzzzzzz-0024-wifi-count-only-final-tx-failures.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/9999-zzzzzzzz-0024-wifi-count-only-final-tx-failures.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/9999-zzzzzzzz-0024-wifi-count-only-final-tx-failures.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+From: ACK72 <acikom72@gmail.com>
+Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:30:00 +0900
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: count only final TX failures
+
+The TX-free header carries each frame's transmission count and final
+status. tx_failed added every retry to the final failure, so it equalled
+tx_retries whenever no frame was lost and overstated real losses
+otherwise. nl80211 defines TX_FAILED as failed packets, and mac80211
+reports frames that failed after all retries. Count the final status only;
+retries remain in tx_retries.
+
+--- a/mt7996/mac.c
++++ b/mt7996/mac.c
+@@ -1308,14 +1308,16 @@
+
+ 			if (!wcid)
+ 				continue;
+
+ 			count = FIELD_GET(MT_TXFREE_INFO_COUNT, info);
+ 			tx_retries = count ? count - 1 : 0;
+-			tx_failed = tx_retries +
+-				!!FIELD_GET(MT_TXFREE_INFO_STAT, info);
++			/* nl80211 and mac80211 count failed packets, not failed
++			 * attempts; retries are reported separately.
++			 */
++			tx_failed = !!FIELD_GET(MT_TXFREE_INFO_STAT, info);
+
+ 			wcid->stats.tx_retries += tx_retries;
+ 			wcid->stats.tx_failed += tx_failed;
+ 			continue;
+ 		}
+
